{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-projective-line-su2","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:projective-line-su2","kind":"example","title":"Projective line for $\\mathrm{SU}(2)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-projective-line-object","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-maximal-torus-su2"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-projective-line-object","tags":["su2","projective-line"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Examples.su2ProjectiveLine","text":"projective-line-su2.md","leanSource":"projective-line-su2.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:projective-line-su2\"></a><p>For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G = \\mathrm{SU}(2)</code>, the quotient is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{P}(V) = \\mathrm{SU}(2)/\\mathrm{U}(1) \\cong \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code>. A point in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code> represents a line in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V = \\mathbb{C}^2</code>. The corresponding function algebra is the polynomial ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}[z]</code> in the affine coordinate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = v_1 / v_2</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/projective-line-su2.md","heading":"Example","number":"4.5.6","page":"b/ex-projective-line-su2","qa":{"counts":{"pass":66,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":48},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Examples.su2ProjectiveLine","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/projective-line-su2.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"